@section 5.3 | Make in India, Start-ups and Entrepreneurs

@q 4:10-11

**Make in India** (25 September **2014**) promotes manufacturing and investment; its logo is a **lion** made of gears. **PLI schemes** (2020) for 14 sectors and the **National Manufacturing Mission** (2025) build on it.

@q 4:12-15

@table
Scheme | Year | For
**Start-up India** | January 2016 | Start-ups: tax breaks, fund of funds, self-certification; India has 1.5 lakh+ recognised start-ups and over 100 unicorns
**Stand-Up India** | April 2016 | Bank loans of Rs. 10 lakh-1 crore to **SC/ST and women** entrepreneurs
**PM Mudra Yojana** | April 2015 | Loans up to **Rs. 20 lakh** (Shishu, Kishore, Tarun, Tarun Plus) for micro units; under the **Ministry of Finance** (Department of Financial Services)
Udyami helpline | 2010 | MSMEs
@end

Start-ups raise early money from **angel investors, venture capital and crowdfunding**. President **Pranab Mukherjee** spoke of "new-age financing" for start-ups at the Festival of Innovation (2016).

