@q 4:77-79

@q 4:86

Labour-intensive industries **employ more workers** per unit of capital. **Industrial relations** involve workers, managers and the state, not consumers. Workers' **participation in management** means a say in **policy decisions**. The four **Labour Codes** (wages, industrial relations, social security, occupational safety) came into force on **21 November 2025**.

@trap
First industrial policy **1948**; joint sector **1956**; licensing from the **IDR Act 1951**; LPG **1991** (Narasimha Rao). **Micro = Rs. 1 crore investment / Rs. 5 crore turnover** (2020 rule). **Abid Hussain** ended SSI reservation. **Stand-Up India = SC/ST and women.** **Mudra = Finance Ministry.** **CSR = 2%, Companies Act 2013.** **NIP = 2019-25**, **Gati Shakti = 2021**. **IIP excludes construction.** **Golden handshake = VRS.** **Tarapore = convertibility.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Industrial policy history is a long-running favourite; the **2019-2025** papers moved to current schemes (Make in India, Mudra, Gati Shakti, NIP, MSME definition, CSR) in statement form. Watch for date traps (2021 vs 2022, 2013 vs 2014).
@end

